# The build context is scripts/g4_pipeline/. Without this file the whole
# directory is shipped to the daemon, including results/ -- 106 committed
# artifacts and the per-run page images, hundreds of MB that no instruction in
# the Dockerfile reads. That does not change the image id (only the copied
# requirements.lock does), but it makes each build upload megabytes of measured
# telemetry, and it means build output lands next to its own input on the daemon
# side.
results/
*.meta.json
*.measured.jsonl

# The harness itself is mounted read-only at run time; driver.py is deliberately
# not baked into the image, so shipping it into the context invites a second,
# stale copy of the same logic.
driver.py
run_measured.sh
build.sh
PIN_MANIFEST.md

# Optional local wheel directory for hosts that cannot reach
# download-r2.pytorch.org from a build container. It is injected with
# PIP_FIND_LINKS, not COPYed, so it must not be in the context.
local-wheels/
